    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "Choosing what fits · 1 · preparation 2",
    "context": "Use this subset of the shopping vocabulary and constructions in a short self-contained situation, preparing for U5-10. Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to compare quantity, suitability and price before making a purchase.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-10-P02-interact-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Explain the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U5-10-P02-interact-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "Choosing what fits · 1 · preparation 2: Present a supported viewpoint about the decision in this account. Refer to a concrete source detail, acknowledge a plausible alternative, and qualify what the evidence cannot establish.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "朋友想买一条围巾，店里的价格比以前便宜。工作人员说，围巾和手套一起买更便宜。朋友只听见便宜，就准备把两件都买下来。\n\n我请他先看看总共需要付多少钱。新的价格是两件东西一起的价格，不是围巾一件的价格，只买围巾也有另一种价格。\n\n朋友最近已经买了一双手套，并不需要再买。他原来以为多拿一件也不用多付钱，仔细看清楚，才知道自己把两种价格弄错了。\n\n工作人员把两种选择写在纸上，让他慢慢考虑。一起买虽然比一件一件买便宜，但只买围巾，总共花的钱还是更少。\n\n朋友最后只买了围巾。他把纸带回家，想提醒自己以后看见价格下降时，先想想需要什么，再看价格，而不是只看哪个数字变小了。\n\n回去的路上，朋友说这次买的东西虽然不多，却都是自己最需要的。我也明白了，先弄清楚花这些钱买什么，比急着决定更有用。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "A concrete source detail supports my position."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I represented the alternative fairly and retained an important qualification."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
